# Model Alignment Rule

`models.yaml` is the **reference** for recommended HuggingFace repos, GPU sizing, and generated manifests. **Live** model routing (which provider/model each pipeline role uses) is configured in the **admin Registry** (Postgres) and synced to LiteLLM — not by editing `models.yaml` on a running cluster. Use admin “Seed from YAML” only to re-bootstrap deployments from the file.

Models are deployed via **OpenShift AI 3** (dashboard or InferenceService YAML), not by Synesis manifests alone.

## When modifying model references:

1. **Update `models.yaml`** with recommended HuggingFace repos and metadata
2. **Update config files** that point at deployed model endpoints:
   - `base/gateway/litellm-config.yaml` — `api_base` for synesis-router, synesis-general, synesis-critic, synesis-coder
   - `base/planner/app/config.py` — default `router_model_url`, `planner_model_url`, `general_model_url`, `critic_model_url`
   - `base/planner/deployment.yaml` — env vars `SYNESIS_ROUTER_MODEL_URL`, `SYNESIS_PLANNER_MODEL_URL`, `SYNESIS_GENERAL_MODEL_URL`, etc.
3. **Remind the user** to deploy models via OpenShift AI 3 and configure endpoints if deployment names differ from defaults (`synesis-router`, `synesis-general`, `synesis-critic`, `synesis-coder`)

## Service URL pattern

`http://<service-name>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:8080/v1`

## vLLM config alignment

When router/general/critic/coder fail to start or OOM: check [vLLM Recipes](https://docs.vllm.ai/projects/recipes/en/latest/) and `docs/VLLM_RECIPES.md` for model-specific args (tensor-parallel-size, max-model-len, tool-call-parser, etc.).

## Yarn runtime (separate from vLLM roles)

**Synesis Yarn** (`base/yarn/`) is the OpenAI-compatible IDE/agent runtime; it is **not** a vLLM InferenceService. Model/provider for Yarn come from Yarn env (e.g. `SYNESIS_YARN_PROVIDER`, `SYNESIS_YARN_MODEL`), not from `models.yaml` pipeline roles. Deployed via `base/yarn` + overlays (`overlays/api`, `overlays/model`), namespace **`synesis-yarn`**.
